    "workspaceNotes": {
      "model": "A well-mixed vessel receives a water–ethanol feed and 5 W of heat. An ideal moving boundary maintains 1 bar; its volume is a result. Start at the local laws and inspect every recorded assumption in the standard right-hand panel. UNIFAC original supplies the common caloric and equilibrium properties. No equilibrium type or phase count is imposed. Momentum is not solved: pressure and feed rate are declared boundaries.",
      "transform": "The deduced total model passes through the identity transformation. It needs no spatial mesh. Scaling of this coupled equilibrium model is not connected yet; this example does not claim to apply it.",
      "solve": "Integrate water amount, ethanol amount and total enthalpy. At every RHS evaluation recover the vessel state from PH equilibrium and the feed enthalpy from its TP state. Positive feed is 0.001 mol/s with equal mole fractions at 320 K; initial amounts are 0.8 and 0.2 mol at 300 K. Run for 60 s. The method compatibility and mathematical plan below come from the Python compiler.",
      "results": "Matter reference: water = 0.8 + 0.0005 t mol; ethanol = 0.2 + 0.0005 t mol. With constant feed conditions and pressure, H(t) = H(0) + (0.001 h_feed + 5) t J. Temperature, volume, phases and enthalpy use the same selected property package; inspect conservation and physical certification with the plots."
